---
title: Paneer and Chickpea Curry
description: Crispy golden paneer cubes and tender chickpeas simmered in a creamy tikka sauce with spinach.
course: main
cuisine: Indian
servings: 2
time required: 30 minutes
prep time: 10 minutes
cook time: 20 minutes
source: https://www.hellofresh.ca/recipes/smart-paneer-and-chickpea-curry-64db8fe82ad1f1e5380fc770
image: https://media.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_1200/hellofresh_s3/image/cari-de-paneer-et-de-pois-chiches-4e2c64df.jpg
tags:
  - vegetarian
  - curry
  - indian
  - weeknight
---

Heat a #large non-stick pan{} over medium-high heat. Cut @paneer{200%g} into 1/2-inch cubes. Add @butter{1%tbsp} and swirl to melt. Add the paneer, season with @salt, @pepper, and @cumin-turmeric spice blend{1.5%tsp}, and pan-fry, turning occasionally, until crispy and golden, ~{4-5%minutes}. Transfer to a plate.

Meanwhile, peel and cut @yellow onion{1/2}(cut into 1/4-inch pieces). Cut @tomato{1}(cut into 1/2-inch pieces). Roughly chop @baby spinach{56%g} and @cilantro{7%g}.

Return the same pan to medium heat. Add @butter{1%tbsp} and swirl to melt. Add the onion and tomato and cook, stirring occasionally, until softened, ~{3-4%minutes}.

Stir in @tikka sauce{0.5%cup} and @vegetable stock powder{1%tbsp} and cook, stirring often, until the sauce thickens slightly, ~{30%seconds}. Add @water{0.5%cup}, @chickpeas{398%mL}(with canning liquid). Bring to a simmer over high heat, then reduce to medium. Cover and cook, stirring occasionally, until the chickpeas are tender and the tomatoes have broken down, ~{8-10%minutes}.

Add the spinach, half the paneer, and half the cilantro. Cook, stirring often, until the spinach wilts, ~{1-2%minutes}. Add more water 2 tbsp at a time if too thick. Season with @salt and @pepper.

Divide the curry between bowls. Top with the remaining paneer and sprinkle the remaining cilantro over top.
